    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (81.55) and **James Wood** (76.28) today, both of whom profile as elite starts given their dynamic platoon edges and immense stolen base upside against relatively vulnerable pitching. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a favorable matchup against Pallante, and with the optimizer identifying a slow delivery from the opposition, his potential for a multi-steal game is maximized. **James Wood** is similarly positioned to exploit a weak 5.64 xERA matchup in a high-scoring park, with his elite xwOBA of 0.433 making him the primary catalyst for our run production. **Mickey Moniak** (64.31) also demands attention; despite a challenging matchup against Greene, his park factor (+14%) and platoon advantage (+14%) create an ideal environment to overperform his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jose Caballero** (42.76) on the bench. While his underlying speed metrics are typically valued heavily in our 5x5 framework, the optimizer favored the higher reliability of **Austin Riley** (44.30) and the specific lineup placement of our middle infielders. **Jose Caballero** remains the first man up, but the lower projected efficiency compared to our starters kept him off the active roster today. Meanwhile, we are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Alex Freeland**, as any shift out of the bottom third of the order would force a re-evaluation of his 45.36 efficiency score. We continue to manage our daily game caps carefully, noting that **Seiya Suzuki** (63.40) must navigate a \"Wind In\" warning, which threatens to dampen his power profile despite a strong batting order advantage.",
